    <!-- Juegos de PC: una carpeta por juego -->
    <string name="folder_games_hint">PC games live one per folder. Pick the root folder that holds them — Elyndra scans it folder by folder and finds each game\'s executable on its own. It also picks up the shortcuts a Windows runtime exports for frontends (.desktop, .steam…), which is what actually starts the game. Or a folder of ID files: one file per game (.iso, .txt, .steam) named after the game and holding only its BannerHub ID.</string>
    <string name="scan_none_folder_games">No games found. Each game needs its own folder with its .exe inside; pick the folder that contains them all, not one game\'s folder. A folder of shortcuts exported from your Windows runtime works too. Or a folder of ID files: one file per game (.iso, .txt, .steam) whose content is just the BannerHub ID.</string>
    <string name="pc_runtime_explainer">%1$s can\'t be handed a game from outside, so Elyndra just opens it — pick the game there, in its own container.</string>
    <string name="pc_shortcut_explainer">%1$s is handed the shortcut it exports for frontends (.desktop, .steam…), not the .exe. Pick the folder where %1$s writes them.</string>
